    "q-161590": {
      "dom_id": "step-q161590",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "Consider the set $A,$ defined by \n\n$$\nA=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,{x}^{2}+4{y}^{2}\\le 16\\}.\n$$\n\nThe boundary of $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n∂A=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\bbox[5px,border: 1px solid black]{\\phantom{AAAAA}}\\,\\}.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?",
      "worked_solution": "The boundary of a set $A,$ denoted $∂A,$ is the set that contains all the boundary points of $A.$\n\nThe set $A$ and its boundary $∂A$ are shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14134863/assets/b1074330fc650cf6af682f173f50943d779819afa59bf5be19edb88def1ef03a.png)\n\nFrom the diagram, the boundary points of $A$ lie on the ellipse ${x}^{2}+4{y}^{2}=16.$ \n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n∂A=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,{x}^{2}+4{y}^{2}=16\\,\\}.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
