    "q-161595": {
      "dom_id": "step-q161595",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14134863/assets/6559dfed58b9456d6eebfd660f7a0d59a60db9db1159561f010f6b7e13e90e5b.png)\n\nConsider the set $A,$ shown above. The boundary of $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n∂A=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,\\bbox[5px,border: 1px solid black]{\\phantom{AAAAA}}\\,\\}.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?",
      "worked_solution": "The boundary of a set $A,$ denoted $∂A,$ is the set that contains all the boundary points of $A.$\n\nThe set $A$ and its boundary $∂A$ are shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14134863/assets/d7293d96b71f573dbdcbfb491646f0e563f8ad1567eab5baaf960533e72d473f.png)\n\nFrom the diagram, the boundary points of $A$ lie on the line $y=2-x.$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n∂A=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,y=2-x\\,\\}.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
